  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Electric Boat reported $11.6B in contract obligations for FY2026 to date, across 333 awards with an average award size of $34.8M. Obligations fell 45.8% year over year for the same fiscal period. Annual obligations show multi-year variation: FY21 was $8.7B, FY22 was $9.4B, FY23 was $10.8B, FY24 was $8.6B, and FY25 was $21.4B. Engineering Services and Ship Building and Repairing are the largest NAICS markets in FY2026 to date, with $7B and $4.6B respectively. Several manufacturing and R&D NAICS appear lower on the list, including Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) at $3.4M and Instruments and Related Products Manufacturing for Measuring, Displaying, and Controlling Industrial Process Variables at $2.4M. Current-year totals are partial because figures are fiscal year to date, and the reported award-value figures in largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables represent total contract values rather than current-year obligations. This summary focuses on obligations, award counts, and the top NAICS markets for FY2026 to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How did Electric Boat's obligations change recently?",
        "body": "Electric Boat obligated $11.6B in FY2026 to date. Obligations fell 45.8% year over year. Annual obligations ranged from $8.6B in FY24 to $21.4B in FY25, showing sizable year-to-year variation. FY21 through FY23 obligations were $8.7B, $9.4B, and $10.8B respectively."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What are Electric Boat's top markets in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "Engineering Services is the largest NAICS market at $7B. Ship Building and Repairing is the second-largest market at $4.6B. R&D and several specialized manufacturing NAICS follow at smaller dollar levels, including Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) at $3.4M and Instruments and Related Products Manufacturing for Measuring, Displaying, and Controlling Industrial Process Variables at $2.4M."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Electric Boat make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "Electric Boat has received $11.6B in contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Electric Boat has 333 awards this fiscal year to date and an average award size of $34.8M. Obligations fell 45.8% year over year, and prior fiscal-year obligations were $8.7B (FY21), $9.4B (FY22), $10.8B (FY23), $8.6B (FY24), and $21.4B (FY25)."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies buy from Electric Boat?",
      "a": "Agency-level buyers are not listed in these figures. The available reporting shows totals, award counts, and NAICS markets for FY2026 to date but does not provide a breakdown by specific federal agency."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Electric Boat sell to the government?",
      "a": "Electric Boat sells engineering, shipbuilding, R&D, and specialized manufacturing to the government. Engineering Services accounts for $7B and Ship Building and Repairing accounts for $4.6B in FY2026 to date. Other reported NAICS include Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) at $3.4M and Instruments and Related Products Manufacturing for Measuring, Displaying, and Controlling Industrial Process Variables at $2.4M."
    },
